      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "In mice, [18F]PB118, a fluorobenzylamine aryl amide with the closest structural similarity to the query, showed excellent brain uptake of 7 %ID/cc by PET, directly demonstrating that this fluorobenzylamine-amide scaffold can achieve meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "N-(N-benzylpiperidin-4-yl)-2-[18F]fluorobenzamide showed good brain uptake in mice, supporting CNS penetration for the query's fluorophenyl amide/amine motif.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "Compound 63, a cyclopropane-containing aryl amide with a basic amine side chain, entered the brain well in rats with an average brain/plasma ratio of 1.9, supporting CNS access for the query's related cyclobutane amide scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "[18F]4-Fluoroclebopride showed approximately 1% ID/brain uptake and a brain-to-blood ratio of about 5 in rats, confirming that fluorinated benzamide/piperidine analogues can cross the BBB effectively.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "Roxatidine, a piperidine-containing amide/ether, showed only trace CSF exposure in humans (CSF:plasma ratio 0-0.089), providing a caution that some related basic amides can have poor CNS exposure, though this molecule is less structurally similar to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted pass: the query's fluorobenzylpyrrolidine cyclobutane carboxamide aligns with multiple fluorobenzylamine/amide analogues showing good in vivo brain uptake; the single low-CSF example is less transferable and outweighed by the consistent supportive direct CNS evidence.",
